.policy "ruff-pyi048-stub-body-multiple-statements" revision 2
.description "Give each function in a stub file a body of exactly one statement such as an ellipsis; stubs only declare types and are never executed."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff PYI048 (flake8-pyi), stubs only: a def whose body has more than one statement, a docstring included.
// Reported at the def's name.
//   def f():               ← PYI048
//       x = 1
//       return x
#include "python/typing.rr"

.violation PYI048(at: node) code "PYI048" "Reduce this stub function's body to a single statement, normally `...`; stub files only declare types and are never executed."
    suppress ruff "PYI048"
PYI048(n) :- def_body(f, b), body_len(b, k), k > 1, field(f, "name", n), in_stub(f).
